Difference Between Rendering Engines
Blink

Blink is a rendering engine developed by Google. It is used in Google Chrome, Microsoft Edge, and Opera. It is fast and supports modern web technologies.

Gecko

Gecko is a rendering engine developed by Mozilla. It is used in Mozilla Firefox and is known for following web standards.

WebKit

WebKit is a rendering engine developed by Apple. It is used in Safari and is optimized for Apple devices like iPhone and Mac.

